[C2C] STATE FINDINGS · ROUND 15
Medium — §2.3 / §10 — the stated revert invariant is impossible with the rest of the spec. “Deleting the single system-theme.css import restores byte-identical pre-change visuals” conflicts with Wave-1 changes that replace or restructure presentation markup: SysStat, SysTag, SysModalBase, bracketed eyebrow markup/classes, and ConfirmModal migration. Removing CSS cannot restore the previous DOM/component tree or necessarily the previous visual layout. §2.3 even concedes that Sys* components merely degrade to an unstyled panel, which directly contradicts “byte-identical pre-change visuals.” Pin the achievable invariant instead: removing the import disables all system-theme CSS and leaves every surface functional/legible, while reverting the Wave-1 opt-in markup/variant changes restores the exact old appearance. Do not make byte-identical appearance from CSS-import removal an acceptance gate.
Medium — §4.1 / §5 / §10 — the one-live-rim rule lacks a runtime ownership mechanism. SysPanel variant="primary" independently emits .sys-rim--live, while both LeftPanel and SysModalBase are allowed to become primary. The prose says LeftPanel is primary “when no modal is open,” but the spec does not define how that state reaches the drawer or who owns arbitration. A component cannot “guarantee only one” merely because current callers are intended to behave. Pin one authority: e.g. shell-level systemPrimarySurface state, or make modal-open state explicitly suppress the drawer modifier. The E2E count is an excellent regression assertion, but it should verify an actual ownership contract rather than substitute for one.
Low — §2.4 guard-test rule 3 needs explicit exceptions for non-selector CSS constructs. “Every selector in system-theme.css contains .sys- or --system” is correct for ordinary style rules, but the file necessarily also contains :root token definitions, @property, @keyframes, @font-face/@import, and @media. A source-scanning test can easily false-fail or become regex-fragile unless the spec states that the anchor requirement applies only to ordinary selector rules, with :root restricted to --sys-* definitions and animation/font at-rules separately allowlisted.
All Round-11 substantive pins are otherwise incorporated: repaint-heavy rims are explicitly restricted; low-effects and reduced-motion are separate; system styling is opt-in with token isolation; shared components use default-safe variants; opaque backing, 2px non-glow focus, non-hue semantics, and scanline discipline are pinned; Vietnamese-safe font fallback is defined; and P14 now requires dense-screen, motion, focus, fallback-font, live-rim-count, and contrast evidence.
[C2C] END
